markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Getting Data Online

When we use <code>fetch()</code>, we’re starting an online request.  

<code>fetch()</code> doesn’t hand you data right away; it hands you something that <em>can later become data</em>.

## Promise States

<div style="display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; max-width:820px; margin:12px 0;">
  <div style="flex:1; min-width:190px; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-top:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,25,118,0.06);">
    <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">Pending</div>
    <div style="margin-top:4px; font-size:13pt; color:#4b5563;">waiting</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex:1; min-width:190px; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-top:4px solid #3fae56; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,25,118,0.06);">
    <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">Fulfilled</div>
    <div style="margin-top:4px; font-size:13pt; color:#4b5563;">success</div>
  </div>
  <div style="flex:1; min-width:190px; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-top:4px solid #d9534f; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,25,118,0.06);">
    <div style="font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">Rejected</div>
    <div style="margin-top:4px; font-size:13pt; color:#4b5563;">failure</div>
  </div>
</div>

<table style="border:1px solid #d8d5f5; border-radius:12px; background:#ffffff; max-width:820px; margin:20px 0; border-collapse:separate; width:100%; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,25,118,0.08);">
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="padding:14px 16px 8px 16px; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:12px 0 0 0;">
      <span style="font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">Common Confusion</span>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background:#ffe3ce; padding:10px 16px; font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; width:150px; vertical-align:top; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF;">
      Misconception
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px 16px; font-size:14pt; vertical-align:top;">
      <code style="font-size:12pt;">fetch()</code> gives me the data.
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background:#ccf1d0; padding:10px 16px 16px 16px; font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; width:150px; vertical-align:top; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:0 0 0 12px;">
      Truth
    </td>
    <td style="padding:10px 16px 16px 16px; font-size:14pt; vertical-align:top;">
      <code style="font-size:12pt;">fetch()</code> returns a <strong>Promise</strong> that may deliver data later.
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

---

## What <code style="background:#E4E2F8; color:#1F1976; padding:2px 8px; border-radius:6px; font-size:13pt;">fetch()</code> Actually Returns

<table style="border:1px solid #d8d5f5; border-radius:12px; background:#ffffff; max-width:820px; margin:12px 0; border-collapse:separate; width:100%; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(31,25,118,0.08);">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:14px 16px 8px 16px; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:12px 0 0 0;">
      <span style="font-weight:700; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">Flow of a fetch request</span>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:4px 16px;">
      <div style="font-family:'Fira Code', ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size:13pt; background:#0b1020; color:#e5e7eb; padding:16px; border-radius:10px; line-height:1.9;">
        fetch(url) &nbsp;→&nbsp; Promise (Pending)<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↳ Fulfilled &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span style="color:#a5f3a5;">Response</span><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;↳ Rejected &nbsp;&nbsp;→&nbsp; <span style="color:#f7bfbf;">Error</span>
      </div>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:12px 16px 16px 16px;">
      <div style="background:#E4E2F8; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 14px; line-height:1.6; font-size:14pt; color:#1F1976;">
        <strong>Important:</strong> When the Promise is fulfilled, you do <em>not</em> get the final data yet. You get a <strong>Response</strong> object.<br>
        That Response can then be turned into usable data (like JSON).
      </div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

---

## Mini Checkpoint

Think about the following and check your answer before moving on.
  
**If <code style= "font-size: 12pt;">fetch()</code> doesn’t give the final data right away, what does it give you immediately?**


<details style="margin:10px 0; border-radius:10px; padding:10px; background:#ececec; max-width:820px;">
  <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:bold;font-size: 12pt;">🔎Check your thinking</summary>
  <div style="padding-top:10px; line-height:1.6;font-size: 12pt;">
    <strong>A Promise.</strong> It starts in the <strong>pending</strong> state and may later be fulfilled (with a <strong>Response</strong>) or rejected (with an <strong>Error</strong>).
  </div>
</details>






MARKDOWN
